 DECISION on srv1: repair kanidm-cert-renew
========================================================================
 PROBLEM DETECTED
   Nobody can log in with a directory account, anywhere.
   Why it matters: The identity server's certificate has expired, so
   every machine refuses to talk to it.

 LIKELY CAUSE  (found by the diagnostic tool: TLS_CERT_EXPIRED)
   The identity server's certificate is past its end date.
   Found on this host: notAfter 2026-11-11T16:32:44Z; collected
   2026-11-11T16:33:11Z; verify expired

 PROPOSED ACTION
   Back up the current certificate and key, issue a new certificate from
   the project's certificate authority, and restart the identity server.

 POTENTIAL DOWNSIDE
   If it is wrong: The identity server restarts, interrupting logins for
   a few seconds. If the certificate authority is unhealthy, the repair
   does not start.
   Undo: The previous certificate and key are saved and put back, with a
   restart, if the check afterwards fails.

 SAY NO IF
   The site is moving the identity server to a different certificate
   authority.

