 DECISION on client2: repair unixd-refresh
========================================================================
 PROBLEM DETECTED
   A person removed from a group can still use that group's access on
   this workstation.
   Why it matters: Access that was taken away still works here until the
   cache is refreshed: a security exposure.

 LIKELY CAUSE  (found by the diagnostic tool: UNIXD_CACHE_STALE)
   This workstation still lists group memberships the identity server
   has removed.

 PROPOSED ACTION
   Mark this workstation's account cache as out of date and re-read the
   person's account, so the removal takes effect now.

 POTENTIAL DOWNSIDE
   If it is wrong: Little risk: it re-reads current data from the
   identity server. The repair refuses if the server is unreachable.
   Undo: Cannot be undone, and does not need to be: it only re-reads
   current data.

   Follows ISSO decision 28.

 SAY NO IF
   The identity server is unreachable from this workstation: fix that
   first.

 If unsure, type no: nothing on client2 changes.
