 DECISION on client2: repair time-resync
========================================================================
 PROBLEM DETECTED
   Authenticator codes are rejected on this workstation, and some secure
   connections fail.
   Why it matters: People who log in with an authenticator code are
   locked out of this machine until its clock is right.

 LIKELY CAUSE  (found by the diagnostic tool: TOTP_TIME_SKEW)
   This host's clock differs from the time source by more than 30
   seconds.
   Found on this host: offset 0.0 s, last source sample 600.0 s vs ;
   threshold 30 s

 PROPOSED ACTION
   Restart the time service and set this workstation's clock to the time
   source now, once, with your approval.

 POTENTIAL DOWNSIDE
   If it is wrong: If the time source itself is wrong, the clock moves
   to the wrong time. The repair refuses to run without a reachable
   source.
   Undo: Cannot be undone, and does not need to be: the old time was
   wrong. Without this step the clock corrects itself in about two
   hours.

   Follows ISSO decision 30.

 SAY NO IF
   The time source itself is in doubt (other machines show clock
   problems too).

