 DECISION on client2: repair selinux-restorecon
========================================================================
 PROBLEM DETECTED
   Logins or the login service fail on this workstation, often with no
   entry in the security log.
   Why it matters: The security system silently blocks the login service
   because some of its files carry the wrong security labels.

 LIKELY CAUSE  (found by the diagnostic tool: SELINUX_LABEL_WRONG)
   Identity-related files on this host carry a security label different
   from the one the policy defines.
   Found on this host: /run/kanidm-unixd: var_run_t (policy says
   kanidm_unixd_var_run_t); /run/kanidm-unixd/sock: var_run_t (policy
   says kanidm_unixd_var_run_t); /run/kanidm-unixd/task_sock: var_run_t
   (policy says kanidm_unixd_var_run_t)

 PROPOSED ACTION
   Put back the security labels the policy defines, only on the identity
   files that differ.

 POTENTIAL DOWNSIDE
   If it is wrong: Little risk: it restores only the labels the
   installed policy defines, on a fixed list of identity paths.
   Undo: The current labels are recorded first and put back if the check
   afterwards fails.

   Follows ISSO decision 12.

 SAY NO IF
   Those labels were set on purpose as a documented exception.

