 DECISION on client2: repair ssh-ca-trust-restore
========================================================================
 PROBLEM DETECTED
   Nobody's SSH certificate login to this workstation works; password
   logins still do.
   Why it matters: People who log in remotely with certificates are
   locked out of this machine.

 LIKELY CAUSE  (found by the diagnostic tool: SSH_CA_NOT_TRUSTED)
   The SSH service here does not trust the project's SSH certificate
   authority (setting missing, empty, or a different key).
   Found on this host: sshd TrustedUserCAKeys: none; no SSH user CA is
   trusted: certificate logins fail

 PROPOSED ACTION
   Trust the project's SSH certificate authority again (only the key
   matching the pinned fingerprint), check the SSH settings are valid,
   then reload the SSH service.

 POTENTIAL DOWNSIDE
   If it is wrong: If the SSH settings are broken in some other way, the
   validity check stops the reload; sessions already open stay open.
   Undo: The previous SSH files (or their absence) are saved and put
   back if the check afterwards fails.

 SAY NO IF
   The site deliberately changed SSH certificate authorities and this
   tool's pinned key is the old one.

